      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2018-june/q5",
      "question": "<p>A student’s attempt to solve the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\log_2 x - \\log_2 \\sqrt{x} = 3\"></span> is shown below.</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2\\log_2 x - \\log_2 \\sqrt{x} = 3\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2\\log_2 \\left( \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x}} \\right) = 3\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>using the subtraction law for logs</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2\\log_2 \\left( \\sqrt{x} \\right) = 3\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>simplifying</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\log_2 x = 3\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>using the power law for logs</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x = 3^2 = 9\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>using the definition of a log</p><p>(a) Identify two errors made by this student, giving a brief explanation of each.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>(b) Write out the correct solution.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p>",
