    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2018-june/q8",
      "question": "<p>A lorry is driven between London and Newcastle.</p><p>In a simple model, the cost of the journey <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"£C\"></span> when the lorry is driven at a steady speed of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v\"></span> kilometres per hour is</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"C = \\frac{1500}{v} + \\frac{2v}{11} + 60\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>(a) Find, according to this model,</p><p>(i) the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v\"></span> that minimises the cost of the journey,</p><p>(ii) the minimum cost of the journey.</p><p>(Solutions based entirely on graphical or numerical methods are not acceptable.)</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></p><p>(b) Prove by using <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2C}{dv^2}\"></span> that the cost is minimised at the speed found in (a)(i).</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>(c) State one limitation of this model.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p>",
