      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2018-june/q9",
      "question": "<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g(x) = 4x^3 - 12x^2 - 15x + 50\"></span></p><p>(a) Use the factor theorem to show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(x + 2)\"></span> is a factor of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g(x)\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>(b) Hence show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g(x)\"></span> can be written in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g(x) = (x + 2)(ax + b)^2\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> are integers to be found.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p><figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:94mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-01-2018-june/q09-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 2. Sketch of the graph of g.\"></figure><p>Figure 2 shows a sketch of part of the curve with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = g(x)\"></span></p><p>(c) Use your answer to part (b), and the sketch, to deduce the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> for which</p><p>(i) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g(x) \\leq 0\"></span></p><p>(ii) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g(2x) = 0\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p>",
